{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why","id":1539967,"title":"Favorite Discipline and why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-06T20:31:31-07:00","id":1539967,"title":"Favorite Discipline and why?","content":"What is your personal favorite discipline and why? It can be because of a set of powers, it\u2019s a part of your favorite clan, the thematics are great, or it\u2019s just dang powerful. Extra points for including specific powers and little stories of moments the discipline was used in your games that really made an impression on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T20:41:53-07:00","id":1539969,"title":"","content":"This is a tough one as I like Obfuscate and Presence equally.<br /> <br /> I like Obfuscate because it's so useful for hiding from danger, learning secrets, creating false images and the more powerful applications can make people forget certain folks or safe houses.<br /> <br /> Presence I like because it's a subtle way to make people like you, gain intelligence, bring your prey to you without them being the wiser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T10:11:44-07:00","id":1539995,"title":"","content":"For me it is a toss-up between Auspex and Dominate (V20).<br /> <br /> Both are hyper efficient in that they don't require blood points to use, they have applications in both combat &amp; social encounters, they can be used without invoking a masquerade violation in front of mortals, they both allow for a character to gain boons from others, and they allow for asymmetrical approaches to problems. <br /> <br /> A Dominate character is one of the most efficient starter builds because you just drop all three dots into Dominate, spend your points for the supporting social skills, and then buy the Generation background and you are more or less completely functional. Using just those levels of Dominate will then allow you to gain boons, get out of fights, make others fight for you, clean up masquerade issues, and gain practically endless amounts of additional Background dots once game play starts. From there you can focus your XP gains into other areas because you are more or less done with Dominate XP spending. The result being that this works with any clan with Dominate as a clan discipline.<br /> <br /> An Auspex character takes longer to build out and often requires specific choices to make work, but once they are rolling full force they tend to upend many stories because they can bypass the standard cat &amp; mouse dynamics of many vampire games. Obfuscate clans lose a lot of their thunder when an Auspex specialist is running around, most mysteries are easily solved, and once you get the higher-level powers it becomes ridiculously easy to gain blackmail information. Alternatively, an Auspex specialist with Aura Reading and a high caliber gun is a nightmare in a pitch-black combat environment, Nos &amp; Malks get so angry when you pick up a shotgun and turn off the lights.<br /> <br /> An example of a potent Auspex build would be a Tremere who at character generation put all three dots into Auspex and then burned bonus points to get the last two dots in it. Since Auspex isn't dependent on Generation, they can freely use their Background points to buy a very powerful Retainer in the form of a loyalist Gargoyle who is combat focused. Since both the Tremere and the Gargoyle reside at the local chantry, which is heavily warded, there is no easy way to get at them. But the character can astral project all over the place and use Telepathy to cause all sorts of havoc. From there the Tremere can generate boons by being an information broker, which leads to gaining Obfuscate, which the character then teaches to the Gargoyle so he can be protected even while out and about. For extra flavor and to throw your poor ST a bone for upending many story plots, grab the Oracular Ability merit so that you can be even more of Seer or Prophet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T11:53:13-07:00","id":1540002,"title":"","content":"Auspex is both the one I find most powerful and most fun to use. Information is the most potent asset you can have, whatever your goal, and no level of Auspex leaves you wanting. And as a player I really like to know things before the others, specially before enemies and rivals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T15:26:22-07:00","id":1540017,"title":"","content":"Two other Disciplines that I have high regard for are Auspex and Protean.<br /> <br /> With Auspex you have effective means of learning about people, the environment and the presence of supernatural beings. With a single touch I can learn from an object what kinds of people have touched it and gain insight and knowledge of dangers us half the battle and you can avoid it.<br /> <br /> Protean I like the usefulness of altering your form to look like animals and be overlooked and being able to sleep into the ground if you can't find a proper dwelling can be a life saver or turning into mist and getting into hard to reach places is a good advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T03:38:45-07:00","id":1540037,"title":"","content":"I'd go with necromancy/mortis. It's got the fun flexibility of thaumaturgy while remaining more 'grounded' with a more reasonable range of powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T04:35:47-07:00","id":1540038,"title":"","content":"Fortitude. I just think there is something subtly horrific and inhuman about someone being able to take a baseball bat to the face without flinching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T08:37:17-07:00","id":1540041,"title":"","content":"Fortitude is a good Discipline to learn and would one of the first physical powers besides Celerity that I would learn after Obfuscate, Presence &amp; Protean were at advanced levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-08-2024, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T17:00:41-07:00","id":1541092,"title":"","content":"Favorite: All of them? Maybe not Fortitude. <br /> <br /> We're they real and I could learn them sans any kind of curse, it would be a toss up between the Nosferatu or Old World Tzimisce spreads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T11:48:55-07:00","id":1541203,"title":"","content":"For me It's a three way toss up for the Malkavian, Ministry and Ravnos Discipline spread InspectorG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T22:46:28-07:00","id":1541955,"title":"","content":"Presence and Dominate.<br /> <br /> You make them so afraid they can't lift a hand against you, and if they do, you can command them to stand down. The two most potent disciplines in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T08:05:54-07:00","id":1549615,"title":"","content":"Can Fortitude be bypassed or \u201cswitched off\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28559-malachy","name":"Malachy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28559_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T20:36:36-07:00","id":1549639,"title":"","content":"VDA20's Serpentis. Beautiful powers and beautiful theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-30T20:49:44-07:00","id":1549659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1540038#post1540038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortitude. I just think there is something subtly horrific and inhuman about someone being able to take a baseball bat to the face without flinching.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually happened to me once; out drinking and some punks tried to rob my drunk and lecherous roommate and I got pissed. A day later at work, my workers asked why one side of my face was a bit swollen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-30T20:52:30-07:00","id":1549660,"title":"","content":"And, when I first started playing, I like the physical ones the most, Fort, Potence, Celerity, but, a vampire with only those disciplines is, essentially a pawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T08:08:34-07:00","id":1549667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1540038#post1540038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortitude. I just think there is something subtly horrific and inhuman about someone being able to take a baseball bat to the face without flinching.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> <br /> I like it so much I made it *better* in my games. Ventrue should be scarier than they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T20:45:20-07:00","id":1549699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Legendre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1549667#post1549667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +1<br /> <br /> I like it so much I made it *better* in my games. Ventrue should be scarier than they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve always thought that the idea of Fortitude was really cool, but in practice it failed to deliver. So I have also house rules the Discipline to make it more effective.<br /> <br /> As for my favorite Discipline, it\u2019s hard to say. Maybe Dominate. It\u2019s so useful and so iconic for vampires. Give orders that must be obeyed, rewrite memories, make people your slaves, possess someone. It does so many cool important things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T01:51:17-07:00","id":1549704,"title":"","content":"I would say that Dominate is probably my favorite Discipline. Its not a combat Discipline but its practicality and use in various situations, including getting out of dangerous situations that could lead to a dangerous fight, is second to none.<br /> <br /> It isn't fool proof or unbeatable but perhaps the most useful one there is for a Cainite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T02:05:59-07:00","id":1549705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1549660#post1549660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, when I first started playing, I like the physical ones the most, Fort, Potence, Celerity, but, a vampire with only those disciplines is, essentially a pawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends a bit on the exact mechanics one uses, and on the table's imagination.<br /> <br /> I once joked with a friend that Potence was a <i>social</i> discipline. If many Intimidation rolls are based on Strength RAW, including how to <i>resist</i> Intimidation, a vampire with high Potence and Willpower can hardly be turned into a pawn. And the attempt is risky on its own.<br /> <br /> Celerity is also very dangerous, since Dexterity (which gets extra dice from Celerity in VDA20) is a horribly broken attribute RAW. I once wrote down how many common roles depended on each of the 9 Attributes, and Dexterity was way ahead of all the other Attributes, closely followed by Strength. It does little to protect you from mental disciplines, but Initiative still helps and it's not like the other disciplines give you extra resistance to being someone's pawn. They give you tools to turn others into pawns, but not to resist. The game system heavily favours those who act <i>first</i>.<br /> I also one calculated that in VDA20 you could do without Obfuscate by maximising Dexterity, Celerity and Stealth instead. It would be more convenient in terms of uses, unless you specifically want to use Obfuscate 3 to change looks.<br /> <br /> Finally, physical disciplines are scaringly objective. The mechanics are straightforward and hard to argue with (though they could be improved). Being hard to kill and highly lethal is one of the key advantages of vampires over humans, everything else is built on top of that, and a vampire who cultivates this talent more than others is quite dangerous. And you don't really need more than 3 dots in Dominate and Presence to do most cool things, so investing in physical disciplines can be quite convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T00:09:25-07:00","id":1549725,"title":"","content":"My two(ish) favourite Disciplines very much reflect my personal biases when it comes to flavour and concept: Auspex and Blood Sorcery (pick your flavour pre-V5).<br /> <br /> For Auspex, it really just comes down to me being the kind of person who loves knowledge for its own sake. If you're that sort, then the power that helps you expand your senses, see through illusions, etc., is just super valuable. I was glad to see other folks mentioning this as a favourite, despite all the other cool powers that you can choose from the list of Disciplines. <br /> <br /> As for Blood Sorcery, that just comes down to always having been drawn to the idea of mage-type characters. Being able to turn a fondness for reading and a philosophical mindset into something that grants you access to a versatile list of abilities largely limited by your imagination is something that just appeals to me more than any narrow set of more intrinsic powers.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that my limited experience with crunch biases my opinions towards more theoretical assessments. I don't have enough actual playtime to assess my choices based on what has paid off for me in practice. But I feel like I would stick with my answers, and focus more on learning how to make the most of the abilities that fit with my preferences rather than focus on the ones with the most payoff from a metagame perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T04:55:18-07:00","id":1549727,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of Chimerstry. It has so many creative practical and subtle uses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T11:56:33-07:00","id":1549779,"title":"","content":"Chimerstry is an underrated Discipline and I'm glad that it's still an option as an Amalgam power and a perfect compliment to what my Malkavian would know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:09:40-07:00","id":1549788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1549705#post1549705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends a bit on the exact mechanics one uses, and on the table's imagination.<br /> <br /> I once joked with a friend that Potence was a <i>social</i> discipline. If many Intimidation rolls are based on Strength RAW, including how to <i>resist</i> Intimidation, a vampire with high Potence and Willpower can hardly be turned into a pawn. And the attempt is risky on its own.<br /> <br /> Celerity is also very dangerous, since Dexterity (which gets extra dice from Celerity in VDA20) is a horribly broken attribute RAW. I once wrote down how many common roles depended on each of the 9 Attributes, and Dexterity was way ahead of all the other Attributes, closely followed by Strength. It does little to protect you from mental disciplines, but Initiative still helps and it's not like the other disciplines give you extra resistance to being someone's pawn. They give you tools to turn others into pawns, but not to resist. The game system heavily favours those who act <i>first</i>.<br /> I also one calculated that in VDA20 you could do without Obfuscate by maximising Dexterity, Celerity and Stealth instead. It would be more convenient in terms of uses, unless you specifically want to use Obfuscate 3 to change looks.<br /> <br /> Finally, physical disciplines are scaringly objective. The mechanics are straightforward and hard to argue with (though they could be improved). Being hard to kill and highly lethal is one of the key advantages of vampires over humans, everything else is built on top of that, and a vampire who cultivates this talent more than others is quite dangerous. And you don't really need more than 3 dots in Dominate and Presence to do most cool things, so investing in physical disciplines can be quite convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the table had a few players that were into One-Upvampireship and I agree, initiative is key, for, encounters, but, not everything has to be an, &quot;Encounter&quot;. They knew about acting first since Cyberpunk. <br /> <br /> I meant that, if you just focus on physical-stats, you're going to miss out on the other aspects of Vampire, which is about control, and if you can't do the controlling, then you character falls in the controlled-category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T20:00:30-07:00","id":1549801,"title":"","content":"Physical Disciplines are useful, but one should focus on really learning the Disciplines of Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate and Presence to gain real power and self mastery.<br /> <br /> Physical Vampire quote &quot; I can hit hard, fast and take a beating.&quot;<br /> <br /> More well rounded Vampire quote. &quot; That's great, but you wasted your energy on breaking that statue thinking it was me and a crew of hunters are just around the corner to take you down.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T03:22:01-07:00","id":1549810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539967-favorite-discipline-and-why?p=1549788#post1549788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the table had a few players that were into One-Upvampireship and I agree, initiative is key, for, encounters, but, not everything has to be an, &quot;Encounter&quot;. They knew about acting first since Cyberpunk.<br /> <br /> I meant that, if you just focus on physical-stats, you're going to miss out on the other aspects of Vampire, which is about control, and if you can't do the controlling, then you character falls in the controlled-category.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair enough, though part of the issue is that you <i>can</i> do the controlling with a wise use of physical power. Ex.: the Warriors of Glycon. Lore-wise, they're the clan leaders of the Setites in VDA20. They are rulers, merchants, generals. Their phylosophy is focused on body and power, but their idea - and clan weakness - is to surpass others and dominate them in a certain arena or type of power. They have Potence, Obfuscate and Serpentis. How could they achieve this with that discipline spread? Combining Obfuscate's information gathering (through invisibility) and manipulation (through Mask of a Thousand Faces, improved by Serpentis 1 facilitating social rolls) advantages with the sheer intimidatory advantages of Potence and Serpentis 3 and 4 - talking about Disciplines alone, without considering other things they might do. And to some extent, depending on how the table plays and how the ST runs social interactions, those combinations can be more effective than Presence and Dominate, if one knows what they're doing.<br /> <br /> The issue is that the rules of social interactions, and also the use of backgrounds, are fuzzy and too open to interpretation. This I think undermines the social game a bit, which is paradoxical since it's a narrative game where acting and social maneuvering are highly emphasises. I think the game system ends up leaving all of that too much to how each table plays, opening the door for more squabbles between players and ST than for actual social maneuvering, except within bounds that the whole table is already comfortable with (which I think is a reduction, not an expansion, of the game potential, and I stopped playing with a local ST as a result and now hear other players are having the exact same problem with him. He thinks it's players who either don't think or are only focused on the rules, while multiple players have observed that he only recognises thoughts and ideas matching his own, which leads to either players giving up thinking and planning and being creative in how they act, or them trying to argue for their idea based on objectively written rules since he won't see our point otherwise).<br /> <br /> In theory most clans have a fair extent of social action, even if they don't have Dominate and Presence in their discipline spread. It's understood that they leverage other advantages to achieve pawn control. The rules being what they are, or STs applying them as they do, creates a bit of issues, leading to Presence and Dominate being overemphasized, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2E seems to do this part of the system better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T18:42:40-07:00","id":1550018,"title":"","content":"Dominate and Prothean are just so goddamn vampirey that I love it!<br /> <br /> Animalism is super cool and underapreciated, Auspex is close behind. Can't not love physical disciplines too, they give real power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-10T19:21:12-07:00","id":1550021,"title":"","content":"I am learning to like the more subtle uses of the Dominate Discipline, but I still prefer Presence overall when it comes to brass tacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}